#. Tag: title
#: filemng.docbook:6
#, no-c-format
msgid "The File Manager"
msgstr "O xestor de ficheiros"

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde;'s file manager is &konqueror;. The &konqueror; home page is located at "
"<ulink url=\"http://www.konqueror.org\">http://www.konqueror.org</ulink> "
"where a &konqueror; specific <acronym>FAQ</acronym> can be found."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I change the appearance of a folder in &konqueror;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Right-click the folder, select <guimenuitem>Properties</guimenuitem>, click "
"on the large icon in the dialog which appears, and choose another icon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the icon displayed for entries in the <guimenu>K Menu</guimenu>, "
"use the <application>Menu Editor</application>, accessed by clicking with "
"the &RMB; on the &kmenu; icon and selecting <guimenuitem>Menu Editor</"
"guimenuitem> from the menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I do non-anonymous &FTP; transfers with &konqueror;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Normally, if you enter a &URL; like <userinput>ftp://<replaceable>ftp."
"example.com</replaceable></userinput>, &konqueror; will attempt an anonymous "
"login to the &FTP; server. If you want to login as a particular user, enter "
"a &URL; like <userinput>ftp://<replaceable>username@ftp.example.com</"
"replaceable></userinput> instead. &konqueror; will ask for your password and "
"connect to the server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I specify the startup folder for &konqueror;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the &RMB;, click on the Home icon and choose <guimenuitem>Properties</"
"guimenuitem>. Under the <guilabel>Application</guilabel> tab you will "
"probably find something like <command>kfmclient openProfile filemanagement</"
"command>; just append <filename class=\"directory\">file:/whereever/you/"
"want</filename> with the folder you would like &konqueror; to start in."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I rename files?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply <mousebutton>right</mousebutton> click on the file and select "
"<guimenuitem>Rename</guimenuitem> or press the keyboard shortcut <keycap>F2</"
"keycap> with a file selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where did the delete entry from my right-click context menu go?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In &kde; 3.4 the delete context menu entries that bypass the trashcan are no "
"longer displayed by default. To enable them, go to "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &konqueror;</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> and select <guilabel>Behaviour</guilabel> in the "
"iconbar to the left. Tick the checkbox <guilabel>Show 'Delete' context menu "
"entries which bypass the trashcan</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How do I configure the programs that &konqueror; uses to open different "
"types of files?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to configure file associations, you should go to the "
"&kcontrolcenter; and choose the item <guimenuitem>File Associations</"
"guimenuitem> under the category <guimenu>KDE Components</guimenu>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Suppose the default <acronym>PDF</acronym> viewer is now &kghostview; and "
"you would prefer to use <application>KPDF</application> as a viewer. You "
"would simply type <userinput>pdf</userinput> in the search box at the top of "
"the dialog, choose <guimenuitem>pdf</guimenuitem> in the "
"<guimenu>application</guimenu> group and move <application>KPDF</"
"application> up. In the <guilabel>Embedding</guilabel> tab you can also "
"choose which component other applications will use to display files (for "
"example, when viewing files in &konqueror; or using &ark;'s embedded viewer)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How can I configure &konqueror; to open files with double-click instead of "
"single-click?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the &kcontrolcenter;, go to <menuchoice><guimenu>Peripherals</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Mouse</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and in the "
"<guilabel>General</guilabel> tab, select <guilabel>Double-click to open "
"files and folders</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When I try to click on a folder in &konqueror;, I get the message: "
"<quote>There appears to be a configuration error. You have associated "
"Konqueror with inode/directory, but it cannot handle this file type.</quote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You need to make sure that the embedding settings for inode/directory are "
"correct:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In &konqueror;, go to <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Konqueror</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and then "
"to the <guilabel>File Associations</guilabel> page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open inode->directory in the tree view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the <guilabel>Embedding</guilabel> tab. Make sure that "
"<guilabel>Left Click Action</guilabel> is set to <guilabel>Show file in "
"embedded viewer</guilabel>, and by default <guilabel>Icon View "
"(konq_iconview)</guilabel> is at the top of <guilabel>Services Preference "
"Order.</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"What are <option>%i</option> and <option>%m</option> in the Execute line?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"They are used by all &kde; applications (since they are implemented in "
"<classname>KApplication</classname> and all good &kde; programs create a "
"<classname>KApplication</classname> object before they even look at the "
"command line arguments)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A standard line for a &kde; application looks like this: "
"<userinput><command>foo</command> <option>... %i %m -caption \\\"%c\\\"</"
"option></userinput>. Pretty confusing, -but it has been designed in that way "
"so that it can integrate legacy, non-&kde; applications as smoothly as "
"possible. &konqueror;, when executing the line above, will extend the "
"command to <userinput><command><replaceable>foo</replaceable></command> "
"<option>-icon something.png -miniicon something_mini.png -caption \\\"The Foo"
"\\\"</option></userinput>. Both the icon and the mini-icon as well as \"The "
"Foo\" are properties defined in the <filename>.desktop</filename> file. If "
"the icons are not defined, they simply default to the executable name "
"<replaceable>foo</replaceable>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This way a user can change these things in &kmenuedit; for his or her "
"applications. The <option>-caption</option> option is important, because no "
"user will accept that the menu item <guimenuitem>Editor</guimenuitem> starts "
"something called <guilabel>kedit-0.9pl4-build47</guilabel>. Instead, he "
"expects a window called <guilabel>Editor</guilabel>. Furthermore these names "
"are localized, <abbrev>i.e.</abbrev> an American user launches "
"<guimenuitem>CD-Player</guimenuitem> and gets a window called <guilabel>CD-"
"Player</guilabel> while a German user launches <guimenuitem>CD-Spieler</"
"guimenuitem> and gets a window called <guilabel>CD-Spieler</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How do I make &konqueror; start up without a menu bar? I can't save a view "
"profile when the menu bar is invisible!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The easiest way to do this is to edit &konqueror;'s configuration file "
"manually. Add the following lines to <filename>~/.kde/share/config/"
"konquerorrc</filename>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: filemng.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[KonqMainWindow]\n"
"MenuBar=Disabled"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid "On restarting &konqueror;, the menubar should be hidden."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<acronym>JPEG</acronym> files no longer show previews in &konqueror; (and "
"I've installed CrossOver Office)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: filemng.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"CrossOver creates new &MIME; types that will override the default image/jpeg "
"and image/jpg times. In &konqueror;, go to <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Konqueror</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>, and "
"then to <guilabel>File Associations</guilabel>. Find the application/x-"
"crossover-jpg and application/x-crossover-jpeg entries, and remove them. "
"Then hit <guibutton>OK</guibutton>. This problem is reported fixed in the "
"latest version of CrossOver."
msgstr ""
